      "data": {
        "html": "<p>Shortcuts in Notes</p><p></p><p>Text sizes</p><p><strong>⌘ 1</strong> = Display size (or begin a line with #)</p><p><strong>⌘ 2</strong> = Headline size (or begin a line with ##)</p><p><strong>⌘ 3</strong> = Subheader size (or begin a line with ###)</p><p><strong>⌘ 4</strong> = Normal size</p><p></p><p>Creating lists</p><p>☐\t<strong>⌘ T</strong> = Checkbox</p><p>•\t<strong>⌘ L</strong> = Bullet point</p><p></p><p>Styling text</p><p><strong>⇧⌘ E</strong> = Highlight Marker</p><p><strong>⌘ B</strong> = <strong>Bold</strong></p><p><strong>⌘ I</strong> = <em>Italic</em></p><p><strong>⌘ U</strong> = <strong>Underline</strong></p><p><strong>⇧⌘ X</strong> = <strong><s>Strikethrough</s></strong></p><p><strong>⌘ ⌫</strong> = Clear styling</p>",
        "color": "yellow",
        "size": "md",
        "rotation": 0
      },
      "width": 824,
      "height": 640
    },
    {
      "id": "5374e766",
      "type": "text",
      "position": {
        "x": -504,
        "y": 120
      },
      "data": {
        "html": "<h1>Summary</h1><p></p><p>Our team wanted to accommodate increasing customer's needs in time series data anomaly detection (tsAD). I helped the team to define the product scope, establish project lifecycle, and design and test the UI from scratch.</p><p>The MVP was adopted by 300+ customers, quickly validating our initial direction. This may not be a big number in consumer section, but for a specialized domain, it was a strong signal that we were solving a real customer need.</p>",
        "size": "md"
      },
      "width": 336,
      "height": 280
    },
